[00:08.89]What happened to the clavichord? | 古钢琴出了什么事？
[00:12.57]We have an old musical instrument. | 我们家有件古乐器。
[00:16.10]It is called a clavichord. | 被称作古钢琴。
[00:18.91]It was made in Germany in 1681. | 它是1681年德国造的。
[00:23.78]Our clavichord is kept in the living room. | 我们这架古钢琴存放在起居室里。
[00:27.31]It has belonged to our family for a long time. | 我们家有这件乐器已经很久了。
[00:31.61]The instrument was bought by my grandfather many years ago. | 这件乐器是我祖父在很多年前买的。
[00:36.42]Recently it was damaged by a visitor. | 最近它被一位客人弄坏了。
[00:39.87]She tried to play jazz on it! | 她用它弹了爵士乐！
[00:42.88]She struck the keys too hard and two of the strings were broken. | 她按键太猛，把两根弦按断了。
[00:48.43]My father was shocked. | 我父亲大为吃惊。
[00:51.32]Now we are not allowed to touch it. | 现在我们不许再碰它。
[00:54.36]It is being repaired by a friend of my father's. | 父亲的一个朋友正在修理它。
